  subjects:
  - Training Part 1
  greetings:
  - 'For your first guideline: look out for anything that is impersonating a real
    company/figure. An example may include a microsoft email, called micronoft365,
    or a google email, called google-security. These should simply be called microsoft.com/google.com,
    instead of some fancy convoluted name. Keep your eyes peeled on the headers,
    as that may be of immense value for detecting phishing scams.'
